# Tick counts on TODO-634.md, with the census that makes them exhaustive: the file carries 7
# top-level boxes and NO indented ones, so ticked + unticked covers every box it has.
ticked_count 2
unticked_count 5
total_boxes 7
indented_boxes 0

# The strict anchor is a line PREFIX ending at REPEAT:, chosen so it survives the required edit
# (which appends to the box) but breaks the instant the box is ticked. The loose anchor is the
# same text without the checkbox marker and is used ONLY to LOCATE the box, so that a ticked box
# still REDs limb (c) while limbs (d) and (e) stay computable.
box_anchor - [ ] **NEW, CARRIED IN FROM SPEC-356b — the §8.1 REPEAT:
box_anchor_loose **NEW, CARRIED IN FROM SPEC-356b — the §8.1 REPEAT:

# Limb (d). The pointer literal is required verbatim in the box's after-text. The outcome tokens
# are the determination vocabulary of the frozen predicate; at least one must appear.
pointer_literal spec356-manifest.md §10
outcome_tokens INDETERMINATE SELECTION FRONTIER THROUGHPUT SCHEDULING
